{
  "slug": "guide/di/creating-and-using-services",
  "title": "Creating and using services",
  "description": "Services are reusable pieces of code that you can share across your Angular application to handle data fetching, business logic, and shared state.",
  "source": "https://angular.dev/guide/di/creating-and-using-services",
  "status": "reviewed",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Services are reusable pieces of code that you can share across your application. You often use them to handle data fetching from a backend server, implement business logic, or manage shared state across different components."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "creating-a-service",
      "text": "Creating a service"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can generate a service using the Angular CLI command:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "terminal",
      "lang": "bash",
      "code": [
        "ng generate service hero"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can also author a service manually by applying the <code>@Injectable()</code> decorator to a TypeScript class:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "src/app/hero.service.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';",
        "",
        "@Injectable({",
        "  providedIn: 'root', // Makes the service available application-wide as a singleton",
        "})",
        "export class HeroService {",
        "  private heroes = ['Windstorm', 'Bombasto', 'Magneta'];",
        "",
        "  getHeroes() {",
        "    return this.heroes;",
        "  }",
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "injecting-a-service",
      "text": "Injecting and using a service"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "In modern Angular, use the <code>inject()</code> function to consume the service in components:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "file": "src/app/hero-list.component.ts",
      "lang": "ts",
      "code": [
        "import { Component, inject } from '@angular/core';",
        "import { HeroService } from './hero.service';",
        "",
        "@Component({",
        "  selector: 'app-hero-list',",
        "  standalone: true,",
        "  template: `",
        "    <ul>",
        "      @for (hero of heroes; track hero) {",
        "        <li>{{ hero }}</li>",
        "      }",
        "    </ul>",
        "  `",
        "})",
        "export class HeroListComponent {",
        "  private heroService = inject(HeroService);",
        "  heroes = this.heroService.getHeroes();",
        "}"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
